,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":176.302064227,"data":"[08:21:52]   [A 1/47] DAPT01EVAL-001 JAIN_TERMINOLOGY (86 tok) \"In J. N. Farquhar's Notes on the Religious Literature of India, ahimsa is defined as the avoidance of all form\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":190.383964131,"data":"[08:22:06]   [A 2/47] DAPT01EVAL-002 JAIN_TERMINOLOGY (84 tok) \"According to Stevenson's Notes on Modern Jainism, Karma is a force that binds souls to the material world, pre\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":204.746711852,"data":"[08:22:20]   [A 3/47] DAPT01EVAL-003 JAIN_TERMINOLOGY (87 tok) 'Stevenson identifies the two great divisions of Jain cosmic time as the Satya Kalpa (true era) and the Avasarp'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":215.214075191,"data":"[08:22:31]   [A 4/47] DAPT01EVAL-004 JAIN_TERMINOLOGY (63 tok) 'Stevenson identifies the Three Jewels as: 1) the Jinas (Tirthankars), 2) the Acharyas (Guru), and 3) the Sthav'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":225.405192805,"data":"[08:22:41]   [A 5/47] DAPT01EVAL-005 STHANAKAVASI_TERMINOLOGY (62 tok) 'According to Stevenson, the Samayika is generally said in the temple by Sthanakavasi Jaina. However, he notes '\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":244.637622498,"data":"[08:23:00]   [A 6/47] DAPT01EVAL-006 STHANAKAVASI_TERMINOLOGY (116 tok) \"According to Stevenson's account of the Sthanakavasi canon, there are 14 Mulagrantha. These are considered to \"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":260.1228479,"data":"[08:23:16]   [A 7/47] DAPT01EVAL-007 STHANAKAVASI_TERMINOLOGY (93 tok) 'Vaiyavacca is a vow that prohibits an ascetic from touching or being touched by any living being, including an'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":291.851658021,"data":"[08:23:47]   [A 8/47] DAPT01EVAL-008 STHANAKAVASI_TERMINOLOGY (192 tok) 'The Terapanthi accept the Sthanakavasi scriptures, excluding the Suvrata and the Sambhuti. They also accept th'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":323.747388209,"data":"[08:24:19]   [A 9/47] DAPT01EVAL-009 PRAKRIT (192 tok) \"पाइय-सद्द-महान्नवो के अनुसार 'अहिंसण' शब्द का अर्थ है 'अहिंसा' या 'अहिंसा का अनुष्ठान'। यह शब्द जैन दर्शन के अ\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":355.570767998,"data":"[08:24:51]   [A 10/47] DAPT01EVAL-010 PRAKRIT (192 tok) \"पाइय-सद्द-महान्नवो में 'उवस्सय' शब्द के लिए 'उपस्थापन' या 'उपस्थिति' दिया गया है। यह शब्द जैन दर्शन के अनुसार \"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":387.355818168,"data":"[08:25:23]   [A 11/47] DAPT01EVAL-011 PRAKRIT (192 tok) \"पाइय-सद्द-महान्नवो में प्राकृत शब्द 'सामइगि' का हिंदी रूप 'सामायिक' दिया गया है, जिसका अर्थ है 'साधु का एक आचा\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":397.24576461,"data":"[08:25:33]   [A 12/47] DAPT01EVAL-012 PRAKRIT (60 tok) \"Woolner considered Ardha-Magadhi as the 'Prakrt par excellence' due to its rich literary tradition and its sig\"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":428.89445427,"data":"[08:26:04]   [A 13/47] DAPT01EVAL-013 HINDI (192 tok) 'उत्तराध्ययन सूत्र की रचना भगवान महावीर के दशम गणधर श्री अनन्तनाथ भगवान ने नागरोद नगरी में अपने गुरु श्री भगवान'\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":460.669531576,"data":"[08:26:36]   [A 14/47] DAPT01EVAL-014 HINDI (192 tok) 'उत्तराध्ययन शब्द का शाब्दिक अर्थ है-- अध्ययन का उत्तर, अध्ययन का उत्तर देना। इस शब्द का व्यवहार आगमों में भी ह'\n"}
